              "the 5 unguarded v2 controllers are intentionally public (slots reserve/available, routing-form submit, OAuth2 authorize, timezones, health)",
              "all 37 publicProcedure usages are intentionally-public surfaces (public booking-page slots, signup/email verification, i18n, timezones, public profiles, feature flags)",
              "v1 index.ts (welcome message) and docs.ts (OpenAPI spec) are intentionally public; event-types/_utils/* are authorization helper functions, not resource endpoints",
              "markHostAsNoShow (packages/trpc/server/routers/publicViewer/markHostAsNoShow.handler.ts) is an intentionally-public anonymous publicProcedure: the in-code comment (L9-L10) explicitly documents it as a 'completely anonymous and public endpoint' used by non-Cal attendees via an email link, gated by knowledge of the high-entropy bookingUid (capability-URL pattern). Per the CWE-862 misclassification guard, intentionally-public endpoints are recorded in ruledOut rather than emitted as findings."
            ],
            "status": "complete"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
